$col[218,163,0]{Food Efficiency} affects:
$col[218,163,0]{Food Efficiency} affects the percentage of $col[0,180,0]{FEPs} and $col[255,192,128]{Hunger} you gain from food.
$col[185,185,185]{Note that your Table + Chair, Account Verification and Subscription Status also affect FEP and Hunger gain.}

$col[128,128,255]{Energy} gain is *NEVER* affected by $col[218,163,0]{Food Efficiency}, or anything else!
$col[185,185,185]{You will always gain the full energy provided by all foods.}

Enabling this will cause cave dust tiles:
Enabling this will cause cave dust tiles to show the number of potential cave-ins surrounding them, just like in Minesweeper.
$col[218,163,0]{Note:} $col[185,185,185]{If a cave-in has been mined out, the tiles surrounding it will still drop cave dust, and they will still show a number on the ground. The cave dust tiles are pre-generated with the world. That's just how Loftar coded it.}
$col[218,163,0]{Note:} $col[185,185,185]{You can still pick up the cave dust item off the ground. The numbers are affected only by the duration of the falling dust particles effect (aka dust rain), which can be set below}

$col[200,0,0]{NOTE:} $col[185,185,185]{There's a bug with the falling dust particles, that we can't really "fix". If you mine them out on a level, the same particles can also show up on different levels or the overworld. If you want them to vanish, you can just relog, but they will despawn from their original location too.}

Opens the $col[218,163,0]{Translations}:
Opens the $col[218,163,0]{Translations} folder in your client folder.

Anything you put in $col[218,163,0]{Translations \ <language> \ *.json} overrides the translation shipped with the client, so your corrections survive client updates.

$col[185,185,185]{Adding a new folder there adds a new language to the list above. Deleting one removes it.}

This is the name of the .wav sound file:
This is the name of the .wav sound file that will be played when the alarm is triggered.
The file must be present in the "AlarmSounds" folder.
$col[185,185,185]{You don't need to include the file extension in this box, but it must always be a .wav file!}

Writes every piece of text the client co:
Writes every piece of text the client could not translate to $col[218,163,0]{Translations \ <language> \ missing \ *.json}, as ready-to-fill-in entries.

Translate the values, then move the entries into the matching file one folder up.

$col[185,185,185]{Only useful if you are working on a translation. Leave it off otherwise.}
